WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.548
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Newspaper Class, level two.

2
00:00:05.848 --> 00:00:09.664
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.964 --> 00:00:17.295
Unit eleven: Cryptocurrency Basics. Today you will talk about risk with may well, run the risk of and is liable to.

4
00:00:17.595 --> 00:00:20.491
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:21.433 --> 00:00:25.305
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:26.150 --> 00:00:27.221
Blockchain.

7
00:00:28.217 --> 00:00:32.352
Blockchain means a shared digital record that cannot easily be changed.

8
00:00:32.950 --> 00:00:35.716
Blockchain records every transaction in order.

9
00:00:36.317 --> 00:00:38.609
Your turn. Say: Blockchain.

10
00:00:41.467 --> 00:00:42.770
Blockchain.

11
00:00:43.517 --> 00:00:44.878
Digital currency.

12
00:00:45.883 --> 00:00:49.590
Digital currency means money that exists only in electronic form.

13
00:00:50.183 --> 00:00:52.601
A digital currency can be sent worldwide.

14
00:00:53.217 --> 00:00:55.985
Your turn. Say: Digital currency.

15
00:00:58.833 --> 00:01:00.218
Digital currency.

16
00:01:00.983 --> 00:01:02.159
Volatility.

17
00:01:03.150 --> 00:01:06.891
Volatility means how quickly and sharply a price goes up and down.

18
00:01:07.483 --> 00:01:10.087
High volatility makes planning difficult.

19
00:01:10.683 --> 00:01:13.997
Your turn. Say: Volatility.

20
00:01:16.833 --> 00:01:18.055
Volatility.

21
00:01:18.817 --> 00:01:19.969
Crypto wallet.

22
00:01:20.983 --> 00:01:25.015
Crypto wallet means a program or device that stores digital currency.

23
00:01:25.617 --> 00:01:28.011
She lost access to her crypto wallet.

24
00:01:28.617 --> 00:01:31.710
Your turn. Say: Crypto wallet.

25
00:01:34.567 --> 00:01:35.777
Crypto wallet.

26
00:01:36.517 --> 00:01:37.785
Decentralized.

27
00:01:38.783 --> 00:01:41.967
Decentralized means not controlled by one central authority.

28
00:01:42.583 --> 00:01:45.291
A decentralized system has no single owner.

29
00:01:45.883 --> 00:01:48.896
Your turn. Say: Decentralized.

30
00:01:51.733 --> 00:01:53.118
Decentralized.

31
00:01:53.883 --> 00:01:54.699
Mining.

32
00:01:55.683 --> 00:02:00.005
Mining means using computers to confirm transactions and create new coins.

33
00:02:00.617 --> 00:02:03.011
Mining uses a great deal of electricity.

34
00:02:03.617 --> 00:02:05.700
Your turn. Say: Mining.

35
00:02:08.567 --> 00:02:09.545
Mining.

36
00:02:10.283 --> 00:02:11.807
Exchange platform.

37
00:02:12.817 --> 00:02:17.324
Exchange platform means a website where digital currencies are bought and sold.

38
00:02:17.917 --> 00:02:20.172
The exchange platform closed suddenly.

39
00:02:20.783 --> 00:02:23.529
Your turn. Say: Exchange platform.

40
00:02:26.367 --> 00:02:28.111
Exchange platform.

41
00:02:28.850 --> 00:02:29.898
Regulation.

42
00:02:30.883 --> 00:02:34.264
Regulation means official rules that control an activity.

43
00:02:34.850 --> 00:02:37.430
Stronger regulation may protect investors.

44
00:02:38.017 --> 00:02:41.006
Your turn. Say: Regulation.

45
00:02:43.867 --> 00:02:45.112
Regulation.

46
00:02:45.900 --> 00:02:49.632
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:50.483 --> 00:02:57.234
Visal, a news analysis says 'Investors may well lose money, and they run the risk of fraud.' What do these phrases do?

48
00:02:58.350 --> 00:03:05.753
They express risk. 'May well' means it is quite likely. 'Run the risk of' is followed by -ing or a noun.

49
00:03:06.850 --> 00:03:08.524
Any other risk language?

50
00:03:09.617 --> 00:03:18.213
'Is liable to' also means likely, often for something negative: 'Prices are liable to fall suddenly because of volatility.'

51
00:03:19.317 --> 00:03:21.641
Why is this crucial for crypto news?

52
00:03:22.750 --> 00:03:35.782
A decentralized currency has little regulation, so a crypto wallet or exchange platform may fail without warning. Honest reporting shows both opportunity and danger.

53
00:03:36.933 --> 00:03:38.364
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:39.217 --> 00:03:44.061
Grammar focus: Risk language: may well and run the risk of and liable to.

55
00:03:44.361 --> 00:03:45.582
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:46.283 --> 00:03:48.620
Investors may well lose all their money.

57
00:03:49.517 --> 00:03:53.525
Anyone using an unregulated platform runs the risk of losing funds.

58
00:03:54.417 --> 00:03:56.625
Prices are liable to fall suddenly.

59
00:03:57.567 --> 00:04:07.339
Run the risk of + -ing: runs the risk of losing. Is liable to + base verb: is liable to fall. May well + base verb means quite likely.

60
00:04:08.083 --> 00:04:11.374
Be careful! Don't say: Prices are liable fall.

61
00:04:13.333 --> 00:04:16.192
Say: Prices are liable to fall.

62
00:04:16.492 --> 00:04:18.085
Add 'to' after liable.

63
00:04:18.900 --> 00:04:21.483
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:22.267 --> 00:04:23.895
Digital Money, Real Risk.

65
00:04:24.195 --> 00:04:30.397
A digital currency runs on blockchain, a decentralized record that no single bank controls.

66
00:04:31.400 --> 00:04:36.952
Mining and exchange platforms make trading possible, but a crypto wallet can be hacked or lost.

67
00:04:37.967 --> 00:04:42.509
Prices are liable to swing wildly, and investors may well lose their savings.

68
00:04:43.500 --> 00:04:47.079
Because regulation is still limited, buyers run the risk of fraud.

69
00:04:48.067 --> 00:04:52.144
Anyone considering crypto should invest only what they can afford to lose.

70
00:04:53.233 --> 00:04:57.444
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:58.283 --> 00:05:00.712
Investors blank well lose all their money.

72
00:05:01.012 --> 00:05:04.283
A, may. B, might to. C, are.

73
00:05:07.833 --> 00:05:09.473
The answer is A: may.

74
00:05:10.617 --> 00:05:14.915
Anyone using an unregulated platform runs the risk of blank funds.

75
00:05:15.215 --> 00:05:18.416
A, losing. B, lose. C, to lose.

76
00:05:21.967 --> 00:05:23.850
The answer is A: losing.

77
00:05:25.017 --> 00:05:27.933
How quickly a price goes up and down is its blank.

78
00:05:28.233 --> 00:05:32.073
A, volatility. B, mining. C, regulation.

79
00:05:35.633 --> 00:05:38.097
The answer is A: volatility.

80
00:05:39.250 --> 00:05:41.133
Choose the correct sentence.

81
00:05:41.433 --> 00:05:47.664
A, Prices are liable fall.. B, Prices are liable to fall.. C, Prices liable to falling are..

82
00:05:51.200 --> 00:05:54.059
The answer is B: Prices are liable to fall..

83
00:05:55.217 --> 00:05:58.993
According to the reading, buyers should invest only what they can afford to…

84
00:05:59.293 --> 00:06:02.412
A, lose. B, borrow. C, hide.

85
00:06:05.967 --> 00:06:07.734
The answer is A: lose.

86
00:06:08.933 --> 00:06:12.038
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:06:12.883 --> 00:06:16.868
What risks come with investing in a highly volatile digital currency?

88
00:06:25.683 --> 00:06:27.044
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:06:27.344 --> 00:06:48.610
The biggest risk is volatility: the price may fall by half in a few days, so investors may well lose their savings. There is also a risk of fraud or hacking, because regulation is limited and a crypto wallet can be lost. For these reasons, I would invest only a small amount that I could afford to lose.

90
00:06:48.910 --> 00:06:50.689
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:06:51.583 --> 00:06:57.800
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and risk language: may well and run the risk of and liable to.

92
00:06:58.100 --> 00:07:02.575
Today's value is prudence. Think carefully about risks before you act.

93
00:07:02.875 --> 00:07:05.458
See you in Unit twelve. Goodbye!

94
00:07:05.758 --> 00:07:09.107
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

